# JavaScript & Data

## Data model (`data/products.js`)
- `CATEGORIES`: `{ slug, name, description }` — slug drives URLs and icon lookup
- `PRODUCTS`: `{ id, name, category, description, sku, moq, priceRange, featured, specs, customization, color }`
- `category` on products must match a category `slug`
- Product `color` is used for gradient placeholder images (initials overlay)

## Icons (`js/icons.js`)
- `CATEGORY_ICONS` keyed by category slug
- Always use `renderCategoryIcon(slug, className)` — never inline emojis

## Main app (`js/main.js`)
- IIFE with `"use strict"` — no modules/build step
- `basePath` is `".."` only inside `/categories/`, otherwise `"."`
- Header/footer rendered on `DOMContentLoaded`
- Page init keyed off `document.body.dataset.page`

## Adding products
Edit `PRODUCTS` in `data/products.js` only. Grids, modals, and contact dropdown populate automatically.

## Product modal
Opened by clicking `.product-card` or keyboard Enter/Space. Quote buttons link to:
```
contact.html?product=${encodeURIComponent(product.name)}
```

## Do not
- Introduce bundlers, TypeScript, or npm dependencies without explicit request
- Duplicate product/category data in HTML files
- Break script load order (products → icons → main)
